# Run CI Checks Before Declaring Done

After making ANY code changes (Rust, config files, workflows), you MUST run the relevant CI checks locally before considering the task complete. Never rely on remote CI to catch issues.

## Rust Changes (CLI / Library)

After modifying any `.rs` file in `src/` or `tests/`, or `Cargo.toml`:

```bash
cargo fmt --all
cargo clippy -p dima -- -D warnings
cargo test -p dima
```

Always run `cargo fmt` FIRST (it can change formatting that clippy then checks), then clippy, then tests.
Use `-p dima` explicitly — never `--workspace` — because the `dima-gui` crate requires
system GUI libraries (egui/wgpu) that may not be available in all environments.

## Documentation Changes (docs/)

After modifying anything in `docs/`:

```bash
cd docs && pnpm install && pnpm build
```

## Workflow Changes (.github/workflows/)

Validate YAML syntax and review the workflow logic manually. Check that referenced paths, actions versions, and environment variables are correct.
